steps.human:
For anything data-backed, the system drafts — or extends — the one canonical mock-data set for those entities: realistic records the rest of the draft is built on, never a duplicate dataset.

I/O boundary: The output is a *.mock.json artifact. Entity records remain dataset-defined objects; the outer artifact schema does not establish their domain field types.

Contract fields and examples (generated)
Consumes:
  SOURCE-REVIEWED DOCUMENTATION: Source-reviewed templates/agents/pt-classifier.md S4 prompt contract; no runtime registration or automatic prompt/schema parity.
  classifier/component: string (required)
  classifier/entities: array (required)
  Schema: [classifier](docs/product-truth/schemas/pt-classifier-output.schema.json)
Produces:
  mock_data/id: string (required)
  mock_data/component: string (required)
  mock_data/version: integer (optional)
  mock_data/readiness: string (required)
  mock_data/entities/*/fields: object (required)
  mock_data/entities/*/records: array (required)
  Schema: [mock_data](docs/product-truth/schemas/mock-data.schema.json)

Input illustrative classifier projection; not an execution receipt — classifier; illustrative; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "component": "ux-prototyping",
  "entities": [
    "Ac"
  ]
}

Output illustrative mock_data projection; not an execution receipt — mock_data; illustrative; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "id": "leafcutter/feature-review",
  "component": "ux-prototyping",
  "readiness": "draft",
  "version": 1,
  "entities": {
    "Ac": {
      "fields": {
        "id": "string; stable acceptance criterion identifier"
      },
      "records": [
        {
          "id": "ACD-300"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

For each screen the request implies, the system drafts a mockup populated from that mock data, so the person sees the actual screens with real-looking content rather than a description.

I/O boundary: The *.mockup.json record registers a screen and optional HTML path. HTML rendering itself is a file artifact; null renders means no rendered page.

Contract fields and examples (generated)
Consumes:
  mock_data/id: string (required)
  mock_data/entities: object (required)
  Schema: [mock_data](docs/product-truth/schemas/mock-data.schema.json)
Produces:
  mockup/id: string (required)
  mockup/screen: string (required)
  mockup/title: string (required)
  mockup/entities: array (required)
  mockup/mock_data_ref: string (optional)
  mockup/renders: null|string (required)
  mockup/readiness: string (required)
  Schema: [mockup](docs/product-truth/schemas/mockup.schema.json)

Input illustrative mock_data projection; not an execution receipt — mock_data; illustrative; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "id": "leafcutter/feature-review",
  "entities": {
    "Ac": {
      "fields": {
        "id": "string; stable acceptance criterion identifier"
      },
      "records": [
        {
          "id": "ACD-300"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

Output illustrative mockup projection; not an execution receipt — mockup; illustrative; selected fields only; full required/defaulted fields in linked contract:
{
  "id": "leafcutter/feature-review",
  "screen": "feature-review",
  "title": "Review the feature",
  "entities": [
    "Ac"
  ],
  "renders": null,
  "readiness": "draft",
  "mock_data_ref": "leafcutter/feature-review"
}
